{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>Like a yearly hired laborer.</b> So as to add: (Leviticus 25:43) \"he shall not rule over him with rigor\"; (Leviticus 25:53) \"before your eyes\"; we do not abandon the ger: (Leviticus 25:53) \"to rule over him with rigor.\""], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites the phrases לא ירדנו בפרך and לרדות בו בפרך from the surrounding verses; 'the ger' appears to be his shorthand for the foreign resident mentioned in Lev. 25:47, rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:33.155914586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}